1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,462
Part four: the Spirit Power cards, the Coyote, and how the game ends.

2
00:00:04,687 --> 00:00:14,177
Whenever you play your Spirit Power card, you choose one of the two face-up Spirit cards, do its actions in order, and put it under its pile. Here are all six.

3
00:00:14,402 --> 00:00:24,019
Bear. Count the stones in the bowl and put them back in the bag. Draw the same number of new stones into the bowl, then take one. Great when the bowl is full of colors you don't need.

4
00:00:24,244 --> 00:00:29,288
Wolf. Draw four stones from the bag into the bowl, then take one. Lots of choice.

5
00:00:29,513 --> 00:00:38,689
Ram. Draw two stones from the bag and place them directly on your board. You must place both if you can. Any you can't place go into the bowl. It's a gamble!

6
00:00:38,914 --> 00:00:44,735
Eagle. Take one stone from the bowl, and after you recover your cards, you get another whole turn.

7
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:52,731
Deer. Take one stone off your own board and put it in the bowl. Then take two stones from the bowl. Use it to fix a mistake or swap a stone.

8
00:00:52,956 --> 00:01:04,501
Bison. Draw three stones into the bowl and take one. Then pick another stone from the bowl and put it back in the bag. It doesn't have to be one you just drew. You can even put a Spirit Stone back to delay the end of the game.

9
00:01:04,726 --> 00:01:13,066
The Coyote. While the Coyote stands on one of your animals, you can't add any stones to it, not even a Spirit Stone, until the Coyote moves away.

10
00:01:13,291 --> 00:01:23,989
There are two ways to move the Coyote. One is the Add Three Stones and Move Coyote card. The other is hidden on the back of your two Take One Stone cards: each shows half of the Coyote.

11
00:01:24,214 --> 00:01:32,206
When both Take One Stone cards are face down, the Coyote picture is complete, and you may move the Coyote onto any animal on your opponent's board.

12
00:01:32,431 --> 00:01:44,521
The end of the game. If at the end of any turn five Spirit Stones are out of the bag, in the bowl or on the boards, the game ends immediately. With the Bison you can return one to the bag before your turn ends to keep the game going.

13
00:01:44,746 --> 00:01:56,709
Add up your points. The player with the most points wins. If it's a tie, the player who currently has the Coyote on their board wins. The trickster pays you back after all! Now watch a full sample game in part five.
